## THE 12 HIGH-VALUE EDGES (2025–2026 meta)

Ranked shortcuts — the cells most likely to be filled and highest-impact right now.
Details/PoC for each in `references/cve-database.md` + `references/advanced-techniques.md`.

| # | Edge (Source → Sink) | Primitive | Class |
|---|----------------------|-----------|-------|
| 1 | URL `?q=` → session/connector data | P2P one-click + trusted-domain exfil | Reprompt / Claudy Day |
| 2 | Email/doc → connector data | zero-click **service-side** IPI | ShadowLeak / AgentFlayer |
| 3 | RAG doc → cross-tenant data | shared vector-DB poisoning | LLM Scope Violation |
| 4 | Web/email → any tool | indirect injection → tool abuse | EchoLeak |
| 5 | Untrusted data → config file → RCE | self-config-write auto-load | CurXecute / YOLO |
| 6 | MCP schema → secret/RCE | full-schema poisoning + Unicode TAG block | FSP |
| 7 | secret-tool + fetch-tool → key exfil | poisoned page chains two tools | CWE-1336 |
| 8 | LLM output → SSRF + env vars | serialization injection | LangGrinch |
| 9 | NL prompt → DB destroy/dump | text→SQL/Cypher injection | CVE-2024-8309 |
| 10| peer agent → downstream takeover | A2A session smuggling | ASI07 |
| 11| any injection → persistent memory | memory poisoning | ASI06 |
| 12| local endpoint → system prompt | unauth `/api/show`, MCP Inspector RCE | CVE-2025-49596 |

